exports[`R7 — capability digest v2 snapshot test digest markdown matches snapshot (changes only when registry does) 1`] = `
"# Slide block capabilities

Generated from the live block library and slide layouts — do not hand-author a copy of this document, it will drift. Every block below is a closed vocabulary entry: pick a \`type\`, fill its declared slots, and never invent a region name, a slot, or a coordinate.

## Color roles

Use role names (e.g. \`accent\`, \`text\`) in slot values — never bare hex.

- **surface**: Default background fill; resolved from theme.
- **surfaceAlt**: Slightly tinted surface for alternating rows or cards.
- **accent**: Primary brand accent for buttons, links, highlights.
- **accent2**: Secondary accent for charts, secondary emphasis.
- **text**: Primary text colour; contrast-solved against the surface (≥ 4.5:1).
- **textMuted**: Secondary text colour for captions, footnotes; contrast-solved (≥ 4.5:1).
- **positive**: Green status colour for growth, success, positive deltas.
- **negative**: Red status colour for decline, errors, negative deltas.
- **warning**: Amber status colour for caution, in-progress, mixed results.
- **neutral**: Grey status colour for neutral or unavailable data.
- **line**: Hairlines, dividers, gridlines; contrast-solved (≥ 1.4:1).
- **scrim**: Dark overlay for text over images; semi-transparent black wash.

## Style

BlockStyleSpec fields (all optional; absent = theme default):

- \`surface: ColorRole | string — block background\`
- \`on: ColorRole | string — foreground colour (derived from surface when absent)\`
- \`accent: ColorRole | string — emphasis colour\`
- \`tone: 'filled' | 'outline' | 'ghost' | 'inverted' | 'gradient' — visual tone\`
- \`radius: RadiusToken | number — corner radius (none | sm | md | lg | xl | pill)\`
- \`padding: SpaceToken | number | [number, number] — inner padding\`
- \`gap: SpaceToken | number — gap between children\`
- \`elevation: 0 | 1 | 2 — shadow level\`
- \`align: 'start' | 'center' | 'end' — content alignment\`
- \`density: 'compact' | 'default' | 'roomy' — visual compactness\`

Gradient shape: \`Paint: { type: 'solid', color } | { type: 'linearGradient', angle, stops: [{color, at}] } | { type: 'radialGradient', cx, cy, stops: [{color, at}] }\`

## Motion

Set \`motion.preset\` on any block. Every preset below plays (no-op excluded).

Motion style: set \`motionStyle\` on the deck or a slide (slide wins) instead of per-block \`motion\`: \`expressive\` for covers, key numbers and section openers; \`subtle\` for dense content; \`static\` for print/handouts.

- **fade** _text-reveal_ — 250ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **fade-up** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **fade-down** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **pop** _badge_ — 250ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **wipe-x** _panel-reveal_ — 350ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **wipe-y** _panel-reveal_ — 350ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **mask-reveal** _panel-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **reveal-down** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **stagger-lines** _text-reveal_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **stagger-children** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **stagger-grid** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **words-in** _text-reveal_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **quote-in** _composite_ — 1000ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: pop → stagger-lines → fade)
- **count-up** _card-resize_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **grow-bars-x** _card-resize_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **grow-bars-y** _card-resize_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **grow-segments** _card-resize_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **draw-path** _success-check_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **draw-axis-then-nodes** _success-check_ — 800ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: draw-path → stagger-children)
- **sweep** _success-check_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **sweep-nodes** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **pop-points** _badge_ — 250ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick, stagger 40ms
- **radiate** _composite_ — 650ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: pop → stagger-children)
- **grow-branches** _success-check_ — 800ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: draw-path → stagger-children)
- **split-in** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **field-in** _text-reveal_ — 400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick
- **title-then-body** _composite_ — 650ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade-up → fade)
- **title-then-split** _composite_ — 800ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade-up → split-in)
- **scrim-then-text** _composite_ — 750ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade → stagger-lines)
- **ken-burns** _ambient_ — 500ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (loops)
- **cover-in** _composite_ — 1400ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade → words-in → fade-up → fade)
- **section-in** _composite_ — 1000ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: pop → wipe-x → fade-up)
- **dashboard-in** _composite_ — 800ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: stagger-children → grow-bars-y)
- **closing-in** _composite_ — 650ms, triggers: withPrevious, afterPrevious, onClick (chains: fade-up → pop)

## Layouts

Region names belong to the layout — pick a \`layout\`, then only use the regions it lists.

| Layout | Regions | Use when |
|---|---|---|
| \`title\` (Title) | \`title\`, \`subtitle\` | Centered title + subtitle, ideal for simple title slides. |
| \`section\` (Section) | \`title\`, \`subtitle\` | Large title + small subtitle for section dividers. |
| \`two-column\` (Two Column) | \`title\`, \`left\`, \`right\` | Left/right split with a title bar — the workhorse layout. |
| \`three-column\` (Three Column) | \`title\`, \`a\`, \`b\`, \`c\` | Equal thirds with a title bar — comparison or feature lists. |
| \`four-up\` (Four Up) | \`title\`, \`q1\`, \`q2\`, \`q3\`, \`q4\` | 2×2 grid with a title bar — feature matrices, quadrants. |
| \`image-left\` (Image Left) | \`title\`, \`image\`, \`text\` | Image (60%) left, text (40%) right — photo + caption. |
| \`image-right\` (Image Right) | \`title\`, \`text\`, \`image\` | Text (40%) left, image (60%) right — text-first image support. |
| \`image-top\` (Image Top) | \`title\`, \`image\`, \`text\` | Image (60%) top, text (40%) bottom — hero image layout. |
| \`image-bottom\` (Image Bottom) | \`title\`, \`text\`, \`image\` | Text (40%) top, image (60%) bottom — caption-over-image. |
| \`grid-3x2\` (Grid 3×2) | \`title\`, \`c1\`, \`c2\`, \`c3\`, \`c4\`, \`c5\`, \`c6\` | 3 columns × 2 rows — gallery, feature cards. |
| \`grid-2x3\` (Grid 2×3) | \`title\`, \`a\`, \`b\`, \`c\`, \`d\`, \`e\`, \`f\` | 2 columns × 3 rows — compact data grid. |
| \`comparison\` (Comparison) | \`title\`, \`left\`, \`right\` | Two equal columns for side-by-side comparison. |
| \`timeline\` (Timeline) | \`title\`, \`timeline\` | Full-width horizontal timeline area with title. |
| \`quote\` (Quote) | \`quote\`, \`attribution\` | Narrowed centered quote with attribution — testimonial slides. |
| \`kpi-row\` (KPI Row) | \`title\`, \`kpi1\`, \`kpi2\`, \`kpi3\`, \`kpi4\` | Title + 4 equal KPI cells — dashboard-style metrics. |
| \`blank\` (Blank) | \`content\` | Single content region, full safe area — maximum flexibility. |

## Blocks

### \`tls.c.agenda\` — Agenda

Agenda or contents slide: numbered items with titles and optional notes. The current topic can be highlighted. _(family: composite; keywords: agenda, toc, table of contents, outline, topics, schedule, items)_

**When:** Use for a table-of-contents or agenda slide listing 3–8 topics. Set \`current\` to highlight the active topic.
**Avoid:** Do not use for more than 8 items (split into two sections), for a dated sequence (use tls.c.steps) or nested in another block: it fills the whole slide.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (title, note) (1–12 items) | 3–8 items. Each title should be 1–6 words. Notes are optional and brief. |
| \`current\` | no | number | Index of the currently highlighted item (0-based). Omit or set to null to highlight none. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_agenda\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.agenda\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Opening\\",
        \\"note\\": \\"Welcome and agenda overview\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Q3 Results\\",
        \\"note\\": \\"Revenue and growth metrics\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Strategy\\",
        \\"note\\": \\"Next quarter priorities\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Q&A\\",
        \\"note\\": \\"Questions and discussion\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"current\\": 1
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.big-stat\` — Big Stat [html]

Big number slide. One enormous headline metric with a short label and optional context line. Use for KPIs, milestones, and hero stats. _(family: composite; keywords: stat, big, number, kpi, metric, hero, headline, count)_

**When:** Use for a single hero statistic — one big number with a label and optional context.
**Avoid:** Do not use for several metrics side by side (use tls.c.kpi-row), for a number inside a layout with other content (use tls.t.hero-number) or nested in another block.

**Parts:** \`value\`, \`label\`, \`context\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`value\` | yes | number | The headline number to display. Any numeric value. |
| \`label\` | yes | text (max 40 chars) | Short label describing the number. 1–4 words, e.g. \\"Total Revenue\\". |
| \`showLabel\` | no | boolean | Toggle the label below the value on/off. |
| \`context\` | no | text (max 60 chars) | Optional supporting line below the label (e.g. \\"vs last quarter\\"). |
| \`showContext\` | no | boolean | Toggle the context line on/off. |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency | Number format: plain (default), compact (1.2K/3.4M), percent (12%), currency (1,234). |
| \`prefix\` | no | text (max 4 chars) | Optional prefix before the number (e.g. \\"$\\", \\"€\\"). Max 4 chars. |
| \`suffix\` | no | text (max 4 chars) | Optional suffix after the number (e.g. \\"%\\", \\"M\\"). Max 4 chars. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_big_stat\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.big-stat\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"value\\": 4200000,
    \\"label\\": \\"Total Revenue\\",
    \\"context\\": \\"vs last quarter\\",
    \\"format\\": \\"compact\\",
    \\"prefix\\": \\"$\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.cards\` — Cards

Row of 2-4 equal cards, each led by an icon, number or image, then title and text. _(family: composite; keywords: cards, pillars, benefits, offerings, three columns, features, icon cards)_

**When:** Three pillars, key benefits or offerings, each with a short paragraph.
**Avoid:** More than 4 items or icon-only entries: tls.c.feature-grid. Plain points: tls.t.bullets.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`cards\` | yes | list of object (icon, number, image, title, text) (2–4 items) | Each: title!, text, and the field named by lead (icon, number or image). |
| \`lead\` | no | enum: icon \\\\| number \\\\| image \\\\| none | What tops each card. |
| \`tone\` | no | enum: surface \\\\| alt \\\\| outline \\\\| accent-first | accent-first fills only the first card. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_cards\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.cards\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"cards\\": [
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"target\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Clear goals\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"One question per session.\\"
      },
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"check\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Honest results\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"What a result shows.\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"lead\\": \\"icon\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.case-study\` — Case study

Success story: challenge, solution and result, with one headline result number. _(family: composite; keywords: case study, success story, reference, project showcase, before after result, customer story)_

**When:** Success stories, project showcases and references.
**Avoid:** A generic 3-point list: tls.c.cards.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`client\` | no | text (max 40 chars) | Name of the client or project. |
| \`challenge\` | yes | text (max 220 chars) | 1-2 sentences: the problem. |
| \`solution\` | yes | text (max 220 chars) | 1-2 sentences: what was done. |
| \`result\` | yes | text (max 220 chars) | 1-2 sentences: the outcome. |
| \`metric\` | no | object (value, label) | Fields: value, label. |
| \`layout\` | no | enum: columns \\\\| rows | rows = full-width bands. |
| \`emphasis\` | no | enum: result \\\\| none | result = accent-filled result. |
| \`showMetric\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showClient\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_case\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.case-study\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"client\\": \\"Vinh University Library\\",
    \\"challenge\\": \\"Long queues at peak hours.\\",
    \\"solution\\": \\"Self-service kiosks and a renewal app.\\",
    \\"result\\": \\"Queues gone, staff moved to study support.\\",
    \\"metric\\": {
      \\"value\\": \\"-80%\\",
      \\"label\\": \\"waiting time\\"
    },
    \\"layout\\": \\"columns\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.chart-insight\` — Chart with Insight

Chart with its key message in a takeaway panel and a source line. _(family: composite; keywords: chart, insight, takeaway, explained chart, so what, annotated chart, source)_

**When:** A chart whose message must be stated explicitly (\\"Revenue doubled after launch\\").
**Avoid:** Several KPIs: tls.c.dashboard. A bare chart: tls.d.line or tls.d.bar.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`chart\` | yes | object (kind, categories, series) | Fields: kind, categories, series[{name, values}]. bar/pie/donut use series[0] only. |
| \`insight\` | yes | richText (max 200 chars) | The message of the chart in 1-2 sentences. |
| \`insightTitle\` | no | text (max 40 chars) | \\"Key insight\\". |
| \`source\` | no | text (max 120 chars) |  |
| \`side\` | no | enum: right \\\\| left \\\\| below |  |
| \`ratio\` | no | enum: 2:1 \\\\| 3:2 \\\\| 1:1 | Chart width : insight width. |
| \`showSource\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_chart_insight\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.chart-insight\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"chart\\": {
      \\"kind\\": \\"line\\",
      \\"categories\\": [
        \\"Q1\\",
        \\"Q2\\",
        \\"Q3\\"
      ],
      \\"series\\": [
        {
          \\"name\\": \\"Users\\",
          \\"values\\": [
            12,
            18,
            27
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"insight\\": \\"Users **doubled** in two quarters.\\",
    \\"source\\": \\"Source: product analytics\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.closing\` — Closing

Closing slide: thank-you title, call to action, contacts and a presenter. _(family: composite; keywords: closing, thank you, questions, end slide, contact, call to action, next step)_

**When:** Last slide: thanks, Q&A, next step, how to reach us.
**Avoid:** A summary of key points: use tls.c.recap.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`title\` | yes | text (max 50 chars) | \\"Thank you\\", \\"Questions?\\". |
| \`text\` | no | text (max 160 chars) |  |
| \`cta\` | no | text (max 40 chars) | Next step, 2-5 words. |
| \`contacts\` | no | list of text (max 60 chars) (0–4 items) | Email, site, handle. |
| \`person\` | no | object (image, name, role) | Fields: image, name, role. |
| \`variant\` | no | enum: centered \\\\| split | split = panel with person and contacts. |
| \`ctaStyle\` | no | enum: button \\\\| link |  |
| \`showCta\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showContacts\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showPerson\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_closing\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.closing\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"title\\": \\"Thank you\\",
    \\"text\\": \\"Questions are welcome.\\",
    \\"cta\\": \\"Book office hours\\",
    \\"contacts\\": [
      \\"lan.tran@example.edu\\"
    ],
    \\"person\\": {
      \\"name\\": \\"Dr. Tran Thi Lan\\",
      \\"role\\": \\"Head of Data Science\\"
    },
    \\"variant\\": \\"split\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.comparison\` — Comparison

Side-by-side columns, each with a title and a list of items, to contrast options, plans or viewpoints. One column can be highlighted as the recommended one. _(family: composite; keywords: comparison, versus, compare, columns, side by side, options, contrast, pros, cons, alternatives)_

**When:** Use to compare 2–3 options, plans, or viewpoints side by side. Set \`highlight\` to draw attention to the recommended column.
**Avoid:** Do not use for more than 3 columns (split into two slides) or for sequential processes (use tls.c.steps).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`columns\` | yes | list of object (title, items) (2–3 items) | 2–3 columns, each with a short title (2–6 words) and 2–6 short items (2–8 words each). |
| \`highlight\` | no | number | Index (0-based) of the column to highlight with accent colour. Omit or null for none. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_comparison\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.comparison\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"columns\\": [
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Build In-House\\",
        \\"items\\": [
          \\"Full control\\",
          \\"Higher upfront cost\\",
          \\"Longer timeline\\"
        ]
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Buy SaaS\\",
        \\"items\\": [
          \\"Quick setup\\",
          \\"Lower upfront cost\\",
          \\"Vendor lock-in risk\\"
        ]
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Hybrid\\",
        \\"items\\": [
          \\"Balanced approach\\",
          \\"Moderate cost\\",
          \\"Flexible roadmap\\"
        ]
      }
    ],
    \\"highlight\\": 2
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.contact\` — Contact

Contact block: an optional person and email, phone, website, address or social lines, each with its icon. _(family: composite; keywords: contact, email, phone, website, address, social, reach us, get in touch)_

**When:** Where to reach the presenter or the organisation.
**Avoid:** A full closing slide: tls.c.closing.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`person\` | no | object (image, name, role) | Fields: image, name, role. |
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (kind, value) (1–6 items) | Each: kind (email, phone, web, address, social), value. The icon follows the kind. |
| \`showPerson\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_contact\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.contact\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"person\\": {
      \\"name\\": \\"Dr. Tran Thi Lan\\",
      \\"role\\": \\"Head of Data Science\\"
    },
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"kind\\": \\"email\\",
        \\"value\\": \\"lan.tran@example.edu\\"
      },
      {
        \\"kind\\": \\"web\\",
        \\"value\\": \\"stats.example.edu\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.cover\` — Cover

Title slide: kicker, title, subtitle, meta; centred, split or over a photo. _(family: composite; keywords: cover, title slide, opening, first slide, intro, lecture title, photo)_

**When:** First slide of a deck or talk.
**Avoid:** Text-only opener with a button: tls.c.hero. Mid-deck sections: tls.c.divider.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`kicker\` | no | text (max 40 chars) |  |
| \`title\` | yes | richText (max 80 chars) | Up to 10 words. |
| \`subtitle\` | no | text (max 140 chars) |  |
| \`meta\` | no | text (max 80 chars) | Presenter, date. |
| \`image\` | no | image |  |
| \`alt\` | no | text (max 160 chars) |  |
| \`logo\` | no | image |  |
| \`variant\` | no | enum: centered \\\\| split \\\\| bleed | split = photo right; bleed = photo behind. |
| \`decoration\` | no | enum: none \\\\| blob \\\\| arc \\\\| dots |  |
| \`showKicker\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showSubtitle\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showMeta\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showLogo\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showImage\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_cover\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.cover\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"kicker\\": \\"Lecture 1\\",
    \\"title\\": \\"Introduction to Applied Statistics\\",
    \\"subtitle\\": \\"From data to decisions\\",
    \\"meta\\": \\"Dr. Tran Thi Lan · 2026\\",
    \\"image\\": \\"/demo/photo-1.svg\\",
    \\"logo\\": \\"/demo/logo-1.svg\\",
    \\"variant\\": \\"split\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.dashboard\` — Dashboard

KPI tiles, one chart and an insight note on one slide. _(family: composite; keywords: dashboard, kpi, overview, monthly review, status, results, metrics)_

**When:** Performance overview: monthly review, project status, business results.
**Avoid:** One number: tls.c.big-stat. One chart with an explanation: tls.c.chart-insight.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`kpis\` | yes | list of object (label, value, delta, sparkline, polarity, format) (2–4 items) | Each: label!, value!, delta, sparkline[], polarity, format. |
| \`chart\` | yes | object (kind, categories, series) | Fields: kind, categories, series[{name, values}]. bar/pie/donut use series[0] only. |
| \`insight\` | no | text (max 160 chars) | One takeaway sentence. |
| \`layout\` | no | enum: kpis-top \\\\| kpis-left |  |
| \`chartRatio\` | no | enum: 2:1 \\\\| 1:1 | Chart width vs insight width. |
| \`showInsight\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_dashboard\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.dashboard\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"kpis\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Revenue\\",
        \\"value\\": 4200000,
        \\"delta\\": 12.5,
        \\"format\\": \\"compact\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"NPS\\",
        \\"value\\": 62,
        \\"delta\\": 4
      }
    ],
    \\"chart\\": {
      \\"kind\\": \\"line\\",
      \\"categories\\": [
        \\"Jan\\",
        \\"Feb\\",
        \\"Mar\\"
      ],
      \\"series\\": [
        {
          \\"name\\": \\"Revenue\\",
          \\"values\\": [
            3.1,
            3.6,
            4.2
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"insight\\": \\"Revenue grew every month.\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.divider\` — Section Divider

Section break: big section number, title and one-line intro. _(family: composite; keywords: divider, section, chapter, part, break, agenda item, transition slide)_

**When:** Between major parts of a deck or chapters of a lecture.
**Avoid:** The first slide: use tls.c.cover.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`number\` | no | text (max 8 chars) | \\"01\\", \\"II\\" or \\"Part 2\\". |
| \`title\` | yes | text (max 60 chars) |  |
| \`subtitle\` | no | text (max 120 chars) |  |
| \`variant\` | no | enum: numeral \\\\| field \\\\| minimal | field = accent background; minimal = no number. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center |  |
| \`showNumber\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showSubtitle\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_divider\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.divider\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"number\\": \\"02\\",
    \\"title\\": \\"Describing data\\",
    \\"subtitle\\": \\"Centre, spread and shape\\",
    \\"variant\\": \\"numeral\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.feature-grid\` — Feature Grid [html]

Grid of feature cells, each with an icon, title, and description. 2–6 cells arranged in 2/3/4 columns. _(family: composite; keywords: feature, grid, capabilities, benefits, icon, tiles, services, highlights)_

**When:** Use to show 2–6 feature highlights in a grid layout — each cell has an icon, title, and short description. Good for capability overviews, service lists, or product feature showcases.
**Avoid:** Do not use for a comparison of options (use tls.c.comparison), for sequential steps (use tls.c.steps) or for 2-4 framed cards with a paragraph each (use tls.c.cards).

**Parts:** \`cell[*].icon\`, \`cell[*].title\`, \`cell[*].desc\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`cells\` | yes | list of object (icon, title, desc) (2–6 items) | List of 2–6 feature cells, each with icon (icon id string), title (short, 1–4 words), and desc (one sentence). Describe features, benefits, or capabilities. |
| \`columns\` | no | number (min 2, max 4) | Number of columns: 2, 3, or 4. Default is 3. |
| \`gap\` | no | number (min 8, max 48) | Gap between cells in slide units. Default 24. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_feature_grid\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.feature-grid\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"cells\\": [
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"zap\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Fast\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Optimised for speed at every layer.\\"
      },
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"shield\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Secure\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"End-to-end encryption by default.\\"
      },
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"globe\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Global\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Deployed across 30+ regions.\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"columns\\": 3,
    \\"gap\\": 24
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.feature-reveal\` — Feature reveal [html]

Grid of 3-6 icon cards (title + one line) that flip in one after another. _(family: composite; keywords: features, cards, benefits, skills, grid, icons, animated)_

**When:** Key benefits, skills or pillars (3-6) on a showcase slide with motionStyle expressive.
**Avoid:** Dense or printed slides (use tls.c.feature-grid); steps in order (use tls.g.chevrons).

**Parts:** \`card[*]\`, \`icon[*]\`, \`title[*]\`, \`text[*]\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (icon, title, text) (3–6 items) | 3-6 cards, each { icon, title, text? }: a 1-4 word title and one sentence. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_reveal\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.feature-reveal\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"rocket\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Nhanh\\"
      },
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"shield\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"An toàn\\"
      },
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"heart\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Thân thiện\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.hero\` — Hero [html]

Opening slide. One idea in the title, no full sentence; subtitle gives date/audience; CTA optional. _(family: composite; keywords: hero, opening, title, cover, splash, intro, landing)_

**When:** Use as a title/cover slide — one idea in the title, date/audience in the subtitle. Pick variant \\"classic\\" for a standard hero, \\"split\\" when you want the title to reveal from two halves sliding in from opposite sides, or \\"gradient-sweep\\" for a decorative background gradient that sweeps in behind the title on reveal.
**Avoid:** Content slides (use tls.t.title); a cover with photo, logo or meta line (use tls.c.cover); nesting: it fills the slide.

**Parts:** \`kicker\`, \`title\`, \`subtitle\`, \`cta\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`kicker\` | no | text (max 60 chars) | Short label above the title: section name, category, or status. 1–4 words. |
| \`showKicker\` | no | boolean | Toggle the kicker label on/off. |
| \`title\` | yes | richText (max 120 chars) | A concise slide title. Bold one key word for emphasis. Never a full sentence. Max 120 chars. |
| \`subtitle\` | no | richText | Supporting line: date, audience, or context. 3–12 words. |
| \`showSubtitle\` | no | boolean | Toggle the subtitle on/off. |
| \`cta\` | no | text (max 40 chars) | Optional button text. Short imperative, 2–4 words. |
| \`showCta\` | no | boolean | Toggle the call-to-action button on/off. |
| \`variant\` | no | enum: classic \\\\| split \\\\| gradient-sweep | Visual style: \\"classic\\" (default) standard hero with staggered part reveal; \\"split\\" split-title reveal where halves slide in from opposite sides; \\"gradient-sweep\\" a decorative gradient sweeps in behind the title on reveal. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_hero\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.hero\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"kicker\\": \\"QUARTERLY REVIEW\\",
    \\"title\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Margin fell on \\"
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"infrastructure\\",
          \\"bold\\": true
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"subtitle\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Q3 FY2026\\"
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"cta\\": \\"\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.image-text\` — Image + text

Image beside or above a text cluster (kicker + title + body). Configurable placement and image ratio. _(family: composite; keywords: image, text, photo, picture, editorial, side-by-side, layout, composite)_

**When:** Use when a slide needs an image alongside or above explanatory text — editorial layouts, feature descriptions, team slides.
**Avoid:** Do not use for an image-only slide (use tls.m.image) or a text-only slide (use tls.t.title + tls.t.body).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`image\` | yes | image | Asset id or URL of the image to display beside or above the text. |
| \`alt\` | yes | text (max 200 chars) | 1–10 words describing what the image shows. |
| \`placement\` | no | enum: left \\\\| right \\\\| top | Where the image sits relative to the text cluster. |
| \`imageRatio\` | no | number (min 0.2, max 0.8) | Fraction of the box given to the image (left/right splits width, top splits height). |
| \`kicker\` | no | text (max 60 chars) | Short label above the title: section name, category, or status. 1–4 words. |
| \`showKicker\` | no | boolean | Toggle the kicker label on/off. |
| \`title\` | yes | text (max 120 chars) | A concise slide title. 3–10 words. Never a full sentence. |
| \`showTitle\` | no | boolean | Toggle the title text on/off. |
| \`body\` | no | text (max 500 chars) | 1–3 sentences of supporting body copy. |
| \`showBody\` | no | boolean | Toggle the body text on/off. |
| \`gutter\` | no | enum: xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl | Gap between the image and the text cluster. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_image_text\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.image-text\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"image\\": \\"hero-photo\\",
    \\"alt\\": \\"Team meeting in conference room\\",
    \\"placement\\": \\"left\\",
    \\"kicker\\": \\"OVERVIEW\\",
    \\"title\\": \\"Our design process\\",
    \\"body\\": \\"We start with research, prototype rapidly, and validate with users before shipping.\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.journey\` — Journey [html]

Milestones on a curved path; the path draws and each node pops as the line reaches it. _(family: composite; keywords: journey, path, milestones, roadmap, stages, timeline, story)_

**When:** A story of 3-6 stages or dates (a programme, a project, a career) told as one path.
**Avoid:** Precise dated schedules (use tls.g.timeline); more than 6 stages (use tls.g.roadmap).

**Parts:** \`path\`, \`node[*]\`, \`label[*]\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`milestones\` | yes | list of object (when, title, text) (3–6 items) | 3-6 items in order, each { when, title, text? }: a date or stage, 2-5 words, one short line. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_journey\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.journey\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"milestones\\": [
      {
        \\"when\\": \\"2024\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Ý tưởng\\"
      },
      {
        \\"when\\": \\"2025\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Thử nghiệm\\"
      },
      {
        \\"when\\": \\"2026\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Triển khai\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.kinetic-title\` — Kinetic title [html]

Big animated title: words rise in one by one, accent rule draws, subtitle last. _(family: composite; keywords: title, cover, opener, section, animated, kinetic)_

**When:** Deck cover or section opener that should feel energetic; pair with motionStyle expressive.
**Avoid:** Content slides (use tls.t.title); a cover with photo or logo (use tls.c.cover).

**Parts:** \`decor\`, \`kicker\`, \`title\`, \`rule\`, \`subtitle\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`kicker\` | no | text (max 40 chars) | Small label above the title: course, event or section, e.g. \\"BÀI GIẢNG 1\\". |
| \`title\` | yes | text (max 80 chars) | The talk or section title, 2-8 words, no full stop. |
| \`highlight\` | no | text (max 40 chars) | Words of the title to colour with the accent; must appear in the title. |
| \`subtitle\` | no | text (max 120 chars) |  |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center |  |
| \`decoration\` | no | enum: orbs \\\\| none |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kinetic\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.kinetic-title\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"kicker\\": \\"TUẦN 1\\",
    \\"title\\": \\"Dữ liệu kể chuyện\\",
    \\"highlight\\": \\"kể chuyện\\",
    \\"subtitle\\": \\"Nhập môn khoa học dữ liệu\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.kpi-row\` — KPI Row

Row of KPI tiles with an equal-width split, each showing value, change and label. _(family: composite; keywords: kpi, row, tiles, dashboard, metrics, numbers, stats)_

**When:** Use to display 2–5 KPI metrics side-by-side in a row. Good for dashboards and summary slides.
**Avoid:** Do not use for a single KPI (use tls.c.kpi-tile) or for more than 5 KPIs (split across slides).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`tiles\` | yes | list of object (value, delta, label, sparkline, polarity, format) (2–5 items) | 2–5 KPI tiles. Each needs a value and label. Use delta for change indicators and sparkline for trend. |
| \`gap\` | no | enum: xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg | Horizontal spacing between tiles. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kpi_row\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.kpi-row\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"tiles\\": [
      {
        \\"value\\": 4200000,
        \\"delta\\": 12.5,
        \\"label\\": \\"Revenue\\",
        \\"polarity\\": \\"upGood\\",
        \\"format\\": \\"compact\\"
      },
      {
        \\"value\\": 3.1,
        \\"delta\\": -0.8,
        \\"label\\": \\"Churn %\\",
        \\"polarity\\": \\"downGood\\",
        \\"format\\": \\"percent\\"
      },
      {
        \\"value\\": 892,
        \\"delta\\": 42,
        \\"label\\": \\"NPS\\",
        \\"polarity\\": \\"upGood\\",
        \\"format\\": \\"plain\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"gap\\": \\"md\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.kpi-tile\` — KPI Tile

Single KPI metric: headline number, change indicator, label, optional sparkline. Polarity-driven colour. _(family: composite; keywords: kpi, tile, metric, number, stat, value, delta, sparkline, dashboard)_

**When:** Use to display a single KPI metric with its value, change indicator, and optional trend line.
**Avoid:** Do not use for several KPIs side by side (use tls.c.kpi-row), for a plain unframed number (use tls.t.hero-number) or for a metric with an icon (use tls.c.stat-card).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`value\` | yes | number (min -1000000000000, max 1000000000000) | The headline metric number. Use a plain number; formatting is applied by the block. |
| \`delta\` | no | number | Change indicator. Positive = improved, negative = declined (relative to polarity). |
| \`showDelta\` | no | boolean | Toggle the change indicator on/off. |
| \`label\` | no | text (max 30 chars) | Metric name. 1–3 words, never a sentence. |
| \`showLabel\` | no | boolean | Toggle the metric label on/off. |
| \`sparkline\` | no | list of number (2–20 items) | 2–20 numbers for a mini trend line. Omit for a single-point metric. |
| \`showSparkline\` | no | boolean | Toggle the sparkline chart on/off. |
| \`polarity\` | no | enum: upGood \\\\| downGood | Which direction is \\"good\\". upGood = higher is better (revenue). downGood = lower is better (churn). |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency | Number formatting hint. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kpi_tile\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.kpi-tile\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"value\\": 4200000,
    \\"delta\\": 12.5,
    \\"label\\": \\"Revenue\\",
    \\"polarity\\": \\"upGood\\",
    \\"format\\": \\"compact\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.objectives\` — Objectives

Learning objectives or goals as a numbered, checked or icon list with an intro line. _(family: composite; keywords: objectives, learning outcomes, goals, aims, by the end, lecture start, workshop)_

**When:** Start of a lecture, workshop or project: what the audience will achieve.
**Avoid:** A list of topics to cover: tls.c.agenda.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`intro\` | no | text (max 120 chars) | \\"By the end of this session you will be able to\\". |
| \`items\` | yes | list of text (max 120 chars) (2–6 items) | Start each with a verb. |
| \`marker\` | no | enum: numbered \\\\| check \\\\| icon |  |
| \`icon\` | no | icon | For marker icon. |
| \`cols\` | no | enum: 1 \\\\| 2 | Two columns for numbered and check. |
| \`showIntro\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_objectives\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.objectives\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"intro\\": \\"By the end you will be able to:\\",
    \\"items\\": [
      \\"Describe a sample\\",
      \\"Choose a fitting chart\\",
      \\"Run a two-sample test\\"
    ],
    \\"marker\\": \\"numbered\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.problem-solution\` — Problem and solution

A problem statement and its solution side by side, joined by an arrow. _(family: composite; keywords: problem, solution, pain point, pitch, proposal, challenge, fix, before and after)_

**When:** Pitch and proposal slides framing a pain point and the answer to it.
**Avoid:** A visual before and after: tls.g.before-after or tls.m.image-compare.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`problem\` | yes | object (title, text) | Fields: title, text. |
| \`solution\` | yes | object (title, text) | Fields: title, text. |
| \`showIcons\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`style\` | no | enum: panels \\\\| callouts | callouts = danger and success notes. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_ps\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.problem-solution\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"problem\\": {
      \\"title\\": \\"The problem\\",
      \\"text\\": \\"Queues of **20 minutes** at peak hours.\\"
    },
    \\"solution\\": {
      \\"title\\": \\"The solution\\",
      \\"text\\": \\"Self-service kiosks: **under 4 minutes**.\\"
    },
    \\"showIcons\\": true,
    \\"style\\": \\"panels\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.profile-card\` — Profile Card

Card with a portrait, name, role, short bio and a contact line; portrait above or beside. _(family: composite; keywords: profile, person, bio, speaker, lecturer, team lead, card)_

**When:** Introducing one person in detail: speaker bio, lecturer, team lead.
**Avoid:** A row of people (use tls.m.avatar-group or a grid of tls.m.avatar); only a name and role (use tls.m.avatar).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`image\` | no | image | Asset id or URL; initials when empty. |
| \`name\` | yes | text (max 40 chars) |  |
| \`role\` | no | text (max 50 chars) | Title and organisation, 1-8 words. |
| \`bio\` | no | text (max 200 chars) | 1-2 sentences. |
| \`contact\` | no | text (max 60 chars) | Email, handle or site. |
| \`layout\` | no | enum: stacked \\\\| side | stacked = portrait above; side = portrait left. |
| \`tone\` | no | enum: alt \\\\| surface | alt = filled card; surface = open. |
| \`showBio\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showContact\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_profile_card\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.profile-card\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"image\\": \\"asset-lan\\",
    \\"name\\": \\"Dr. Tran Thi Lan\\",
    \\"role\\": \\"Head of Data Science\\",
    \\"bio\\": \\"Leads the applied analytics group.\\",
    \\"contact\\": \\"lan.tran@example.edu\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.quiz\` — Quiz

Multiple-choice question with lettered options; the correct answer is highlighted. _(family: composite; keywords: quiz, multiple choice, question, knowledge check, poll, test, answer)_

**When:** Knowledge checks in lectures and training.
**Avoid:** Open questions with a written answer: tls.t.qa.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`question\` | yes | richText (max 200 chars) | One clear question. |
| \`options\` | yes | list of text (max 80 chars) (2–5 items) | Short, parallel answers; lettered A-E automatically. |
| \`answer\` | yes | number (min 0, max 4) | Zero-based index into options (0 = A). |
| \`explanation\` | no | text (max 200 chars) | Why the answer is right. |
| \`layout\` | no | enum: list \\\\| grid | grid = two columns. |
| \`reveal\` | no | enum: shown \\\\| none | shown highlights the answer; none hides it. No click reveal. |
| \`showExplanation\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_quiz\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.quiz\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"question\\": \\"Which measure resists outliers?\\",
    \\"options\\": [
      \\"The mean\\",
      \\"The median\\",
      \\"The range\\"
    ],
    \\"answer\\": 1,
    \\"explanation\\": \\"The median ignores how far the extremes are.\\",
    \\"layout\\": \\"list\\",
    \\"reveal\\": \\"shown\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.quote-image\` — Quote over photo

Large quote set over a full-bleed photo with a dark scrim, with name and role. _(family: composite; keywords: quote, inspirational, full bleed, photo, scrim, statement, big quote)_

**When:** An emotional or inspirational quote as a full slide.
**Avoid:** A customer testimonial with a face: tls.c.testimonial.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`image\` | yes | image |  |
| \`alt\` | yes | text (max 160 chars) | 1-10 words describing the photo. |
| \`quote\` | yes | richText (max 200 chars) | One or two sentences. |
| \`name\` | no | text (max 40 chars) |  |
| \`role\` | no | text (max 50 chars) |  |
| \`anchor\` | no | enum: bottom-left \\\\| center \\\\| left | Where the text sits on the photo. |
| \`scrim\` | no | enum: medium \\\\| strong | strong = darker wash for busy photos. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_quote_image\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.quote-image\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"image\\": \\"/demo/photo-1.svg\\",
    \\"alt\\": \\"Students working together\\",
    \\"quote\\": \\"Statistics lets data speak in sentences.\\",
    \\"name\\": \\"Dr. Tran Thi Lan\\",
