### \`tls.c.recap\` — Recap

Numbered key points to remember, closed by one takeaway line. _(family: composite; keywords: recap, summary, key points, what we learned, takeaways, review, wrap up)_

**When:** End of a section or lecture: what we learned.
**Avoid:** The final thank-you slide: tls.c.closing.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`points\` | yes | list of richText (max 140 chars) (2–5 items) | One sentence each; **bold** the key term. |
| \`takeaway\` | no | text (max 140 chars) | The one thing to remember. |
| \`style\` | no | enum: numbered \\\\| cards | cards = one panel per point. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_recap\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.recap\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"points\\": [
      \\"Describe data with centre and **spread**\\",
      \\"Pick a chart for **one** question\\",
      \\"Intervals describe the **method**\\"
    ],
    \\"takeaway\\": \\"Plot first, calculate second.\\",
    \\"style\\": \\"numbered\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.stat-card\` — Stat Card

KPI on a card: icon, headline value, unit and caption. _(family: composite; keywords: stat, card, kpi, metric, number, composite)_

**When:** Use when you need a single KPI inside a filled card — icon, headline value, unit, and a caption line. Built compositionally from tls.l.card, tls.l.stack, tls.m.icon, and tls.t.hero-number.
**Avoid:** Do not use for several metrics side by side (use tls.c.kpi-row) or for a metric with a change arrow or sparkline (use tls.c.kpi-tile).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`icon\` | no | icon | Icon name from the set (zap, shield, globe, …). |
| \`showIcon\` | no | boolean | Toggle the icon on/off. |
| \`value\` | yes | text | The headline number. Include formatting, e.g. \\"$4.2M\\", \\"67%\\". |
| \`unit\` | no | text | Unit label, 1–4 words. e.g. \\"Annual Revenue\\". |
| \`caption\` | no | text | Short context, 1 line max. e.g. \\"FY2024 total\\". |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency | Number format hint for the renderer. |
| \`emphasis\` | no | enum: default \\\\| accent \\\\| muted | Colour emphasis for the headline number. |
| \`padding\` | no | enum: 3xs \\\\| 2xs \\\\| xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl | Inner padding of the card. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_stat_card\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.stat-card\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"icon\\": \\"zap\\",
    \\"value\\": \\"$4.2M\\",
    \\"unit\\": \\"Annual Revenue\\",
    \\"caption\\": \\"FY2024 total\\",
    \\"format\\": \\"plain\\",
    \\"emphasis\\": \\"accent\\",
    \\"padding\\": \\"md\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.stat-spotlight\` — Stat spotlight [html]

One key number in a progress ring that counts up, label beside it, up to 3 support stats. _(family: composite; keywords: stat, number, kpi, ring, percent, count-up, headline)_

**When:** One number is the point of the slide (a result, a rate, a total); expressive slides.
**Avoid:** Two to five equal metrics (use tls.c.kpi-row); a trend over time (use tls.d.line).

**Parts:** \`ring\`, \`value\`, \`label\`, \`context\`, \`stat[*]\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`value\` | yes | text (max 12 chars) | The number as it reads, unit included: \\"92%\\", \\"1.250\\", \\"4,6/5\\". |
| \`label\` | yes | text (max 40 chars) |  |
| \`context\` | no | text (max 100 chars) |  |
| \`progress\` | no | number (min 0, max 100) | How much of the ring fills, 0-100; for a percentage use the same number. Default 100. |
| \`stats\` | no | list of object (value, label) (0–3 items) | 0-3 smaller numbers, each { value, label }. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_spot\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.stat-spotlight\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"value\\": \\"87%\\",
    \\"progress\\": 87,
    \\"label\\": \\"Tỉ lệ hoàn thành\\",
    \\"stats\\": [
      {
        \\"value\\": \\"312\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Sinh viên\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.steps\` — Steps

Process or timeline of numbered steps with titles and optional descriptions. Arranges steps horizontally or vertically with thin connectors between them. _(family: composite; keywords: steps, process, timeline, flow, workflow, sequential, phases, roadmap, numbered)_

**When:** Use to show a process, workflow, or timeline with 2–8 numbered steps that the audience reads in sequence.
**Avoid:** Do not use for a compact strip inside a region (use tls.g.steps), for a plain list (use tls.t.bullets) or for fewer than 2 steps (use tls.t.title).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`steps\` | yes | list of object (title, desc) (1–12 items) | 2–6 steps, each 2–8 words in the title. Description is optional, 1–2 sentences. |
| \`orientation\` | no | enum: horizontal \\\\| vertical | Layout direction: horizontal (left to right) or vertical (top to bottom). |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_steps\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.steps\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"steps\\": [
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Plan\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Define scope and requirements\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Build\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Implement the solution\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Ship\\",
        \\"desc\\": \\"Deploy to production\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"orientation\\": \\"horizontal\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.team\` — Team

Grid of team members with photo, name, role and optional bio. _(family: composite; keywords: team, people, speakers, committee, staff, lecturers, research group, who we are)_

**When:** Team, speakers, committee, research group.
**Avoid:** One person: tls.c.profile-card. Faces only: tls.m.avatar-group.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`people\` | yes | list of object (image, name, role, bio) (2–8 items) | Each: name!, role, bio, image (initials when empty). |
| \`cols\` | no | enum: auto \\\\| 2 \\\\| 3 \\\\| 4 | auto picks from the count. |
| \`card\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| card | card = filled panel per person. |
| \`showBio\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_team\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.team\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"people\\": [
      {
        \\"name\\": \\"Dr. Tran Thi Lan\\",
        \\"role\\": \\"Head of Data Science\\",
        \\"bio\\": \\"Leads the analytics group.\\"
      },
      {
        \\"name\\": \\"Nguyen Van An\\",
        \\"role\\": \\"Senior lecturer\\",
        \\"bio\\": \\"Teaches inference.\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.c.testimonial\` — Testimonial [html]

Pull-quote testimonial with attribution. Quote text with speaker name, role, and optional avatar. Use for social proof, customer quotes, or endorsements. _(family: composite; keywords: testimonial, quote, pull-quote, endorsement, social-proof, attribution)_

**When:** Use for a customer quote, testimonial, or endorsement — quote text with speaker name, role, and optional avatar.
**Avoid:** Do not use for a plain pull quote without a named person (use tls.t.quote) or for an unattributed insight (use tls.t.takeaway).

**Parts:** \`quote\`, \`avatar\`, \`name\`, \`role\`

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`quote\` | yes | richText (max 500 chars) | The testimonial quote. 1–3 sentences. Bold key phrases for emphasis. |
| \`name\` | yes | text (max 60 chars) | Speaker's full name. 2–4 words. |
| \`role\` | yes | text (max 80 chars) | Speaker's title or position. 2–8 words. |
| \`avatar\` | no | text (max 200 chars) | Avatar image URL (https:) or asset id. Optional; shows initials when absent. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_testimonial\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.c.testimonial\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"quote\\": \\"This product transformed how our team works. We shipped 3× faster in the first quarter.\\",
    \\"name\\": \\"Jane Doe\\",
    \\"role\\": \\"VP of Engineering\\",
    \\"avatar\\": \\"\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.area\` — Area Chart

Area chart: overlapping, stacked or 100% stacked fills over ordered categories on a zero baseline. _(family: data; keywords: area, stacked, volume, composition, time, chart)_

**When:** Volume over time, composition over time (stacked).
**Avoid:** Precise comparison of series (use tls.d.line).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`categories\` | yes | list of text (max 24 chars) (2–24 items) | Ordered x labels (periods). |
| \`series\` | yes | list of object (name, values) (1–6 items) | One entry per series; values match categories. |
| \`mode\` | no | enum: overlap \\\\| stacked \\\\| percent | stacked adds series up; percent shows shares. |
| \`curve\` | no | enum: linear \\\\| monotone |  |
| \`opacity\` | no | enum: soft \\\\| solid |  |
| \`gridlines\` | no | enum: major \\\\| none |  |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency |  |
| \`legend\` | no | enum: top \\\\| bottom \\\\| right \\\\| none |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_area\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.area\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"categories\\": [
      \\"2022\\",
      \\"2023\\",
      \\"2024\\",
      \\"2025\\"
    ],
    \\"series\\": [
      {
        \\"name\\": \\"Web\\",
        \\"values\\": [
          30,
          38,
          46,
          58
        ]
      },
      {
        \\"name\\": \\"Mobile\\",
        \\"values\\": [
          12,
          20,
          31,
          44
        ]
      }
    ],
    \\"mode\\": \\"stacked\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.bar\` — Column Chart

Column or horizontal bar chart of one series on a zero baseline, with gridlines and an optional highlighted bar. _(family: data; keywords: chart, bar, column, data, graph, vertical, horizontal)_

**When:** Use to compare values across categories — 1–20 bars, single series. Set orientation to horizontal when category labels are long.
**Avoid:** Do not use for parts of a whole (use tls.d.donut), for several series, or for a single headline number (use tls.t.hero-number).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`categories\` | yes | list of text (1–20 items) | Category labels along the X axis. |
| \`series\` | yes | series of number (max 6) | Numeric values for each bar. Use null/NaN for missing data. |
| \`highlightIndex\` | no | number (min -1) | Index of the bar to highlight with accent color. -1 = none. |
| \`orientation\` | no | enum: vertical \\\\| horizontal | vertical = columns (default); horizontal = bars with category labels on the left, best for long labels. |
| \`title\` | no | text (max 120 chars) | Chart title, shown above the chart area. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_bar\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.bar\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"categories\\": [
      \\"Q1\\",
      \\"Q2\\",
      \\"Q3\\"
    ],
    \\"series\\": [
      64,
      64,
      61
    ],
    \\"highlightIndex\\": 2,
    \\"title\\": \\"Revenue by Quarter\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.bubble\` — Bubble Chart

Scatter plot with circle area for a third value, optional labels and size legend. _(family: data; keywords: bubble, portfolio, three variables, size, market, scatter)_

**When:** Portfolio views (market size by growth by share).
**Avoid:** Two measures only (use tls.d.scatter).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`points\` | yes | list of object (x, y, r, label) (3–30 items) |  |
| \`sizeLegend\` | no | boolean | Reference circles at the right. |
| \`gridlines\` | no | enum: major \\\\| none |  |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency |  |

\`\`\`json
{
