### \`tls.d.compare-table\` — Comparison Table

Options as columns, criteria as rows, with ticks, crosses or dot ratings and a highlighted winner. _(family: data; keywords: compare, matrix, features, competitors, versus, tick, rating)_

**When:** Us vs competitors, plan features, tool selection.
**Avoid:** Free-form pros and cons (tls.c.comparison). Prices: tls.d.pricing.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`options\` | yes | list of text (max 24 chars) (2–5 items) | Column headers: the things compared. |
| \`criteria\` | yes | list of text (max 40 chars) (2–12 items) | Row labels, one per row of cells. |
| \`cells\` | yes | list of list of text (max 30 chars) | cells[criterion][option]: yes, no, partial, 1-5 or short text. |
| \`cellKind\` | no | enum: check \\\\| rating \\\\| text | check: ticks and crosses; rating: dots; text: as written |
| \`winner\` | no | number (min -1) |  |
| \`zebra\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`density\` | no | enum: default \\\\| compact |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_compare\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.compare-table\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"options\\": [
      \\"Ours\\",
      \\"Rival\\"
    ],
    \\"criteria\\": [
      \\"Offline mode\\",
      \\"Open API\\",
      \\"SSO\\"
    ],
    \\"cells\\": [
      [
        \\"yes\\",
        \\"no\\"
      ],
      [
        \\"yes\\",
        \\"partial\\"
      ],
      [
        \\"yes\\",
        \\"yes\\"
      ]
    ],
    \\"winner\\": 0
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.donut\` — Donut Chart

Donut chart with colored slices. _(family: data; keywords: chart, donut, pie, data, visualization)_

**When:** Use to display proportional data in a donut chart format.
**Avoid:** Do not use for detailed values or many categories (use tls.d.bar), or for a table of exact figures.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`slices\` | no | list of object () (0–6 items) | Data slices for the donut chart. Max 6 slices; excess grouped into \\"Other\\". |
| \`total\` | no | number | Total value for percentage calculation. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_donut_1\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.donut\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"slices\\": [
      {
        \\"value\\": 30,
        \\"color\\": \\"accent1\\"
      },
      {
        \\"value\\": 25,
        \\"color\\": \\"accent2\\"
      },
      {
        \\"value\\": 25,
        \\"color\\": \\"accent3\\"
      },
      {
        \\"value\\": 20,
        \\"color\\": \\"accent4\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"total\\": 100
  },
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.funnel-chart\` — Funnel Chart

Funnel or bar stages sized by value, with the percentage lost between stages. _(family: data; keywords: funnel, conversion, pipeline, stages, drop-off, sales)_

**When:** Conversion pipelines with real numbers.
**Avoid:** A qualitative funnel without values (use tls.g.funnel).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`stages\` | yes | list of object (label, value) (3–7 items) | Ordered from widest to narrowest, real counts. |
| \`shape\` | no | enum: funnel \\\\| bars | bars = left-aligned bars. |
| \`showDropoff\` | no | enum: percent \\\\| none |  |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_funnel\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.funnel-chart\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"stages\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Visits\\",
        \\"value\\": 5000
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Leads\\",
        \\"value\\": 900
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Deals\\",
        \\"value\\": 120
      }
    ]
  }
}
