### \`tls.d.slope\` — Slope Chart

Slope chart: one line per item between a start and an end column, with values and names. _(family: data; keywords: slope, before after, rank change, two points, rise, fall)_

**When:** Change between exactly two points for several items.
**Avoid:** Many time points (use tls.d.line).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`startLabel\` | yes | text (max 20 chars) | Left column, e.g. 2023. |
| \`endLabel\` | yes | text (max 20 chars) | Right column, e.g. 2025. |
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (name, start, end) (2–10 items) |  |
| \`highlight\` | no | enum: none \\\\| risers \\\\| fallers | Others are dimmed. |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_slope\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.slope\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"startLabel\\": \\"2023\\",
    \\"endLabel\\": \\"2025\\",
