### \`tls.d.stacked-bar\` — Stacked Bar Chart

Stacked columns or bars with optional 100% scaling and totals. _(family: data; keywords: stacked, composition, total, share, bar)_

**When:** Composition of a total across categories; with normalize, compare the mix.
**Avoid:** Comparing individual series values (use tls.d.grouped-bar).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`categories\` | yes | list of text (max 24 chars) (2–12 items) | Axis labels, 1-2 words each. |
| \`series\` | yes | list of object (name, values) (2–6 items) | One entry per series; values match categories. |
| \`orientation\` | no | enum: vertical \\\\| horizontal |  |
| \`normalize\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`totals\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`valueLabels\` | no | enum: none \\\\| inside |  |
| \`gridlines\` | no | enum: major \\\\| none |  |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency |  |
| \`legend\` | no | enum: top \\\\| bottom \\\\| right \\\\| none |  |
| \`highlightIndex\` | no | number (min -1) | Category to emphasise; others dim. -1 = none. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_stacked\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.stacked-bar\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"categories\\": [
      \\"2024\\",
      \\"2025\\"
    ],
    \\"series\\": [
      {
        \\"name\\": \\"Product\\",
        \\"values\\": [
          30,
          38
        ]
      },
      {
        \\"name\\": \\"Services\\",
        \\"values\\": [
          18,
          26
        ]
      }
    ],
    \\"totals\\": true
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.stat-compare\` — Stat Compare

Two labelled numbers with a connector and a coloured change pill (percent or absolute). _(family: data; keywords: compare, before, after, versus, change, delta, year)_

**When:** Before vs after, last year vs this year, us vs benchmark.
**Avoid:** More than two values (use tls.c.kpi-row or tls.d.bar).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`left\` | yes | object (label, value) |  |
| \`right\` | yes | object (label, value) |  |
| \`caption\` | no | text (max 100 chars) | One line of context. |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency |  |
| \`delta\` | no | enum: percent \\\\| absolute \\\\| none |  |
| \`polarity\` | no | enum: upGood \\\\| downGood \\\\| neutral | Which direction is good; neutral = no colour. |
| \`connector\` | no | enum: arrow \\\\| vs \\\\| none |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_stat_compare\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.stat-compare\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"left\\": {
      \\"label\\": \\"2024\\",
      \\"value\\": 4200
    },
    \\"right\\": {
      \\"label\\": \\"2025\\",
      \\"value\\": 5460
    },
    \\"format\\": \\"compact\\",
    \\"caption\\": \\"Annual revenue\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.table\` — Table

Table with header, aligned numbers, status dots, ratings and a totals row. _(family: data; keywords: table, grid, rows, columns, spreadsheet, schedule, specs)_

**When:** Exact values in rows and columns (schedules, specs, results).
**Avoid:** Fewer than 3 values (tls.c.kpi-row). Options vs criteria: tls.d.compare-table.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`columns\` | yes | list of object (label, kind, align, width) (1–8 items) | Set kind: number for figures. |
| \`rows\` | yes | list of list of text (max 60 chars) (1–14 items) | One string per column. |
| \`footer\` | no | list of text (max 40 chars) |  |
| \`zebra\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`rules\` | no | enum: horizontal \\\\| head \\\\| none |  |
| \`header\` | no | enum: filled \\\\| bold \\\\| none |  |
| \`emphasisRow\` | no | number (min -1) |  |
| \`emphasisCol\` | no | number (min -1) |  |
| \`density\` | no | enum: default \\\\| compact |  |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency |  |
| \`showFooter\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_table\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.table\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"columns\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Plan\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Seats\\",
        \\"kind\\": \\"number\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Price\\",
        \\"kind\\": \\"number\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"rows\\": [
      [
        \\"Starter\\",
        \\"5\\",
        \\"$49\\"
      ],
      [
        \\"Team\\",
        \\"25\\",
        \\"$199\\"
      ]
    ],
    \\"footer\\": [
      \\"Total\\",
      \\"30\\",
      \\"$248\\"
    ],
    \\"zebra\\": true
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.trend-badge\` — Trend Badge

Pill with a triangle arrow and a signed change, coloured by direction and polarity. _(family: data; keywords: trend, badge, delta, change, arrow, up, down)_

**When:** Annotating a number elsewhere on the slide with its trend.
**Avoid:** A standalone metric (use tls.c.kpi-tile).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`delta\` | yes | number | Signed change; the sign sets the arrow. |
| \`label\` | no | text (max 30 chars) | Short context after the value. |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency |  |
| \`polarity\` | no | enum: upGood \\\\| downGood \\\\| neutral | Which direction is good. |
| \`size\` | no | enum: md \\\\| sm \\\\| lg |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_trend\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.trend-badge\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"delta\\": -3.2,
    \\"format\\": \\"percent\\",
    \\"polarity\\": \\"downGood\\",
    \\"label\\": \\"churn\\"
  }
}
