### \`tls.g.arrow\` — Arrow

A single straight, curved or elbow arrow in four directions with one or two heads and an optional label. _(family: diagram; keywords: arrow, pointer, connector, curved arrow, elbow, flow direction)_

**When:** Pointing from one block to another on a free layout, with a word on the arrow.
**Avoid:** Connecting steps in a process (use tls.g.flow, which draws its own connectors).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`label\` | no | text (max 30 chars) | Optional, 1-4 words, e.g. \\"then\\" or \\"+12%\\". |
| \`kind\` | no | enum: straight \\\\| curved \\\\| elbow |  |
| \`direction\` | no | enum: right \\\\| left \\\\| up \\\\| down |  |
| \`heads\` | no | enum: end \\\\| both \\\\| none |  |
| \`weight\` | no | enum: md \\\\| sm \\\\| lg |  |
| \`tone\` | no | enum: accent \\\\| text \\\\| muted |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_arrow\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.arrow\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"label\\": \\"Then\\",
    \\"kind\\": \\"curved\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.before-after\` — Before and After

Before and after panels joined by an arrow, each with a tag, title, text and optional image. _(family: diagram; keywords: before, after, transformation, redesign, problem, solution, change)_

**When:** Contrast over time: a transformation, redesign or problem turned into a solution.
**Avoid:** Numeric before/after values (use tls.d.stat-compare).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`before\` | yes | object (label, title, text, image) | {label?, title, text?, image?} for the starting state. |
| \`after\` | yes | object (label, title, text, image) | {label?, title, text?, image?} for the result. |
| \`arrow\` | no | enum: arrow \\\\| chevron \\\\| none |  |
| \`emphasis\` | no | enum: after \\\\| none | after = the After panel gets the accent. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_before_after\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.before-after\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"before\\": {
      \\"label\\": \\"Before\\",
      \\"title\\": \\"Manual reports\\"
    },
    \\"after\\": {
      \\"label\\": \\"After\\",
      \\"title\\": \\"Live dashboard\\"
    }
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.bracket\` — Bracket

A curly or square bracket grouping 2-6 items under one label, label at the right, left or top. _(family: diagram; keywords: bracket, brace, group, together, membership, category)_

**When:** Membership: these items together form one thing, named by the label.
**Avoid:** Values that add up (use tls.g.breakdown).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`label\` | yes | text (max 40 chars) | What the items form together, 1-5 words. |
| \`items\` | yes | list of text (max 60 chars) (2–6 items) | The members, short phrases. |
| \`side\` | no | enum: right \\\\| left \\\\| top | Where the label sits relative to the items. |
| \`style\` | no | enum: brace \\\\| bracket | brace = curly, bracket = square. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_bracket\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.bracket\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"label\\": \\"Core team\\",
    \\"items\\": [
      \\"Product lead\\",
      \\"Tech lead\\",
      \\"Design lead\\"
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.breakdown\` — Breakdown

One whole box split into 2-6 parts with values, joined by a curly brace; can show each share. _(family: diagram; keywords: breakdown, split, components, cost, composition, parts of a whole)_

**When:** Parent/child, one level: a cost breakdown or the components of one metric.
**Avoid:** Several levels (use tls.g.tree) or exact proportions to read off (use tls.d.pie).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`whole\` | yes | object (label, value) | The thing being split: {label, value?}, e.g. {label: \\"Total cost\\", value: \\"$120k\\"}. |
| \`parts\` | yes | list of object (label, value, note) (2–6 items) | {label, value?, note?} per part. Values like \\"$40k\\" or \\"25%\\". |
| \`direction\` | no | enum: LR \\\\| TB | LR = whole left, parts right; TB = whole on top. |
| \`showShare\` | no | boolean | Adds each part as % of the sum when every value is numeric. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_breakdown\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.breakdown\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"whole\\": {
      \\"label\\": \\"Total cost\\",
      \\"value\\": \\"$120k\\"
    },
    \\"parts\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"People\\",
        \\"value\\": \\"$70k\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Cloud\\",
        \\"value\\": \\"$30k\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Tools\\",
        \\"value\\": \\"$20k\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.chevrons\` — Chevron Process

Phases as nested arrow segments in a row, with a \\"we are here\\" highlight. _(family: diagram; keywords: chevrons, phases, process, arrows, stages, method)_

**When:** Order: phases of a project or method, with an optional \\"we are here\\".
**Avoid:** Steps that need descriptions longer than one line (use tls.c.steps). Dated phases go in tls.g.roadmap.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`steps\` | yes | list of object (label, text) (3–7 items) | Phases in order, left to right. |
| \`currentIndex\` | no | number (min -1, max 20) | 0-based index of the phase to highlight; -1 for none. |
| \`fill\` | no | enum: gradient \\\\| single \\\\| series | gradient = accent to accent2. |
| \`textPlacement\` | no | enum: inside \\\\| below | below gives longer notes more room. |
| \`showText\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_chevrons\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.chevrons\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"steps\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Discover\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Research the need\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Design\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Shape the concept\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Build\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Make it real\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Launch\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Release and learn\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"currentIndex\\": 1
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.cycle\` — Cycle

Steps arranged on a ring with arrows that loop back to the first step. _(family: diagram; keywords: cycle, loop, pdca, lifecycle, feedback, circular)_

**When:** Cycle: continuous loops such as PDCA, a product lifecycle or a feedback loop.
**Avoid:** A process with a clear end (use tls.g.chevrons or tls.g.steps).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`steps\` | yes | list of object (label, text, icon) (3–6 items) | Steps in loop order, the first sits at the top. |
| \`center\` | no | text (max 30 chars) | Name of the loop. |
| \`direction\` | no | enum: clockwise \\\\| counter |  |
| \`nodeStyle\` | no | enum: circle \\\\| card | circle = numbered or icon node with the label outside. |
| \`arrowStyle\` | no | enum: arc \\\\| none |  |
| \`showCenter\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showText\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_cycle\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.cycle\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"steps\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Plan\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Set the goal\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Do\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Try the change\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Check\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Measure it\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Act\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Keep what works\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"center\\": \\"PDCA\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.flow\` — Flowchart

Flowchart: steps, decisions, start and end joined by labelled arrows; unknown ids are reported. _(family: diagram; keywords: flowchart, flow, decision, branch, algorithm, approval)_

**When:** Order with branches: decision logic, algorithms, approval paths.
**Avoid:** A straight sequence (use tls.g.steps or tls.g.chevrons).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`nodes\` | yes | list of object (id, label, kind) (2–12 items) |  |
| \`edges\` | yes | list of object (from, to, label) (1–16 items) | Every from/to must be a node id. |
| \`direction\` | no | enum: LR \\\\| TB | LR = left to right, TB = top to bottom. |
| \`routing\` | no | enum: elbow \\\\| straight |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_flow\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.flow\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"nodes\\": [
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"a\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Request\\",
        \\"kind\\": \\"start\\"
      },
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"b\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Valid?\\",
        \\"kind\\": \\"decision\\"
      },
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"c\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Process\\"
      },
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"d\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Reject\\",
        \\"kind\\": \\"end\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"edges\\": [
      {
        \\"from\\": \\"a\\",
        \\"to\\": \\"b\\"
      },
      {
        \\"from\\": \\"b\\",
        \\"to\\": \\"c\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Yes\\"
      },
      {
        \\"from\\": \\"b\\",
        \\"to\\": \\"d\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"No\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.funnel\` — Funnel

Narrowing stages from broad to focused, with a note per stage and no numbers. _(family: diagram; keywords: funnel, stages, narrowing, selection, pipeline)_

**When:** Order with narrowing: marketing funnel, selection process (no numbers).
**Avoid:** Funnels with real values (use tls.d.funnel-chart).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`stages\` | yes | list of object (label, text) (3–6 items) | Broadest stage first. No numbers needed. |
| \`orientation\` | no | enum: vertical \\\\| horizontal |  |
| \`notes\` | no | enum: side \\\\| inside | side = beside (vertical) or below (horizontal). |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_funnel_g\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.funnel\\",
