### \`tls.g.hub-spoke\` — Hub and Spoke

A central hub with 3-8 satellite cards on connecting lines, full circle or fanned over a half circle. _(family: diagram; keywords: hub, spoke, ecosystem, satellites, core, modules, stakeholders)_

**When:** Centre/satellite: an ecosystem, stakeholders around a product, a core with modules.
**Avoid:** Ordered loops (use tls.g.cycle) or parent/child levels (use tls.g.tree).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`hub\` | yes | object (label, icon) | The centre: {label, icon?}. |
| \`spokes\` | yes | list of object (label, text, icon) (3–8 items) | Satellites {label, text?, icon?}, clockwise from the top. |
| \`layout\` | no | enum: circle \\\\| half | half = spokes fan over the top half, hub at the bottom. |
| \`connector\` | no | enum: line \\\\| arrow-out \\\\| arrow-in \\\\| none |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_hub\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.hub-spoke\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"hub\\": {
      \\"label\\": \\"Platform\\"
    },
    \\"spokes\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Web\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Mobile\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"API\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.iceberg\` — Iceberg

An iceberg split at the waterline: a few visible items on the tip, more hidden items underneath. _(family: diagram; keywords: iceberg, hidden, visible, symptoms, root causes, waterline)_

**When:** Contrast of the visible (symptoms, results) against the hidden (causes, effort).
**Avoid:** Two equal sides (use tls.g.pros-cons).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`above\` | yes | object (label, items) | {label, items[1-4]}: what everyone sees. |
| \`below\` | yes | object (label, items) | {label, items[1-6]}: what is hidden. |
| \`waterline\` | no | enum: third \\\\| half | third = the tip takes a third of the height. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_iceberg\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.iceberg\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"above\\": {
      \\"label\\": \\"Seen\\",
      \\"items\\": [
        \\"Late deliveries\\"
      ]
    },
    \\"below\\": {
      \\"label\\": \\"Hidden\\",
      \\"items\\": [
        \\"Unclear ownership\\",
        \\"Manual handoffs\\"
      ]
    }
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.layers\` — Layers

Stacked horizontal layers, each with a label, note and icon, flat or as slanted slabs. _(family: diagram; keywords: layers, stack, architecture, tech stack, osi, tiers)_

**When:** Level: layered architectures and stacks such as app/services/data or the OSI model.
**Avoid:** Narrowing or ranked levels (use tls.g.pyramid).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`layers\` | yes | list of object (label, text, icon) (2–7 items) | Top layer first. {label, text?, icon?}. |
| \`style\` | no | enum: flat \\\\| perspective | perspective = slanted slabs. |
| \`notes\` | no | enum: side \\\\| inside | side = notes beside the stack, inside = in the bar. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_layers\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.layers\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"layers\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Application\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"What users touch\\"
      },
