### \`tls.l.overlay\` — Overlay

Layered children z-stacked in the same box. _(family: layout; keywords: overlay, layer, stack, z-index)_

**When:** Use to layer children on top of each other (backgrounds, watermarks).
**Avoid:** Do not use for sequential layout (use tls.l.stack or tls.l.row) or for a plain background fill (use tls.l.field).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`children\` | no | blocks (allow: layout, text, data, diagram, composite, media) | Child blocks layered z-stack style (last child on top). |

